======================================================================
GATEMATE – ADVANCED ASSEMBLY GUIDE
Modular 3D-Printed Connector System for FPV Gates
======================================================================
Product Status: Prototyping Phase 
Target Hardware: Standard 20mm PVC Electrical Conduits (Baumarkt)
Document Version: 1.1 (Beta)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PRODUCT OVERVIEW
-------------------
GateMate is designed to make DIY FPV drone racing gates affordable,
lightweight, and highly portable. By replacing expensive retail
corner brackets with custom 3D-printed connectors, you can build
infinite track layouts using cheap 20mm PVC pipes from your local
hardware store.
Whether you are blasting through your basement with a 65mm Tiny Whoop
or tearing up a field with a 6S 5-inch freestyle quad, GateMate
connectors are optimized to withstand heavy crashes without breaking.
2. ADVANCED 3D PRINTING SETTINGS (CRASH-RESISTANT)
--------------------------------------------------
To ensure your gates don't shatter upon high-velocity impacts, do NOT
use standard slicing profiles. Follow these strength-optimized settings:
* Material Recommendations:
- PETG: Excellent outdoor durability, high flexibility (bends
instead of snapping upon impact). Highly recommended for 5-inch
gates.
- PLA: Easy to print. Great for Whoop tracks Also works good for 5-inch.
* Slicer Configuration:
- Perimeters (Walls): Minimum 4-5 layers. (More walls = more strength!)
- Top/Bottom Layers: 4 layers minimum.
- Infill Percentage: 30% to 45%.
- Infill Pattern: Gyroid.
- Print Temperature: Print at the higher end of your filament's
spec sheet to maximize layer adhesion.
- no supports: the prints are optimized so modern printers can print them
without supports.
3. REQUIRED HARDWARE & MATERIALS
--------------------------------
To complete a standard square or arch gate, you will need:
* PVC Pipes: Standard 20mm outer diameter (OD) plastic conduits.
* Tools: A basic hacksaw or a pipe cutter to cut the PVC tubes.
* Sandpaper: To smooth out the cut edges of the PVC pipes for an
easier fit into the 3D prints.
4. ASSEMBLY & FITMENT TIPS
--------------------------
* Friction Fit: The connectors are engineered with tight tolerances
so the pipes stay in place without glue.
* Easy Disassembly: If the fit is too tight due to printer
over-extrusion, slightly sand down the outside of the PVC pipe ends
or use a heat gun to gently warm the 3D print before inserting.
* Portability: Do not glue the joints! Leave them as a friction fit
so you can pack down an entire 5-inch gate setup into a backpack.
5. ROADMAP & UPCOMING FEATURES
------------------------------
The GateMate ecosystem is constantly evolving during this prototyping
phase. Future releases will include:
- 90-Degree Corner Matrix Connectors
- 45-Degree Sharp Angle Brackets (for aggressive racing lines)
- Weighted T-Base Mounts for asphalt or indoor sports halls
- Official STL listings on Cults3D and Printables Store
